{"seq":2,"slug":"design-systems","title":"设计系统","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/personal-systems/habit-engineering/design-systems","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"trigger-cue-design","title":"触发与提示设计","url":"/l-doc-books/h/personal-systems/habit-engineering/design-systems/trigger-cue-design","wordCount":2801,"readingTime":12},{"seq":2,"slug":"behavior-simplification","title":"行为简化","url":"/l-doc-books/h/personal-systems/habit-engineering/design-systems/behavior-simplification","wordCount":2910,"readingTime":12},{"seq":3,"slug":"reward-feedback-loops","title":"奖励与反馈循环","url":"/l-doc-books/h/personal-systems/habit-engineering/design-systems/reward-feedback-loops","wordCount":3117,"readingTime":13}],"introHtml":"<h1 id=\"设计系统\">设计系统</h1><p>如果说第一章回答了「为什么行为会发生」，本章则回答「如何让行为发生」。我们把行为科学的原理转化为可操作的设计技术。触发与提示设计一文系统梳理了触发的分类（外部/内部）和设计原则——精确到情境、不可忽视、避免疲劳，并探讨了 2026 年从「时间驱动」到「情境感知」的演进趋势。行为简化一文以 Fogg 行为模型 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B=MAP</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">M</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span></span></span></span></span> 为基石，展示了「把行为缩小到不可能失败」的微习惯方法，以及两分钟规则、行为塑造、反向应用（给坏习惯增负）等具体技术。奖励与反馈循环一文深入多巴胺系统和奖励预测误差机制，解释了为什么即时奖励比延迟奖励更能固化行为、内在奖励与外在奖励对长期习惯的不同影响，以及反馈如何与奖励产生叠加效应。</p>\n"}